          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The analogous theory of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+space"} completion of a space
              involves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+groups"} cyclic groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              – written
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
              when regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
              – and/or the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
              instead of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#LurieProper"} Lurie “Proper morphisms”, section 4
            %p
              For the relation of that to completion see remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationToCompletion"}
              below.
            %p Hence beware the subtle but crucial difference in what a subscript means, depending on which symbol is being subscribed and whether there are parenthesis or not:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}
                  \: inverting all primes except
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
                  \: quotient by
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
                  \:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
                  at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h3#local_groups Local groups
          #TLocalGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is said to be
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-local
              if the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{th}
              power map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to G
              is a bijection for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in \neg T
          #CharacterizationOfAbelianLocalGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              and is generally written additively as multiplication by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is
                  = succeed "-local;" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  admits a structure of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                  (necessarily unique);
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\otimes \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
                  of order
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is equal to zero for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in\neg T
          .num_prop
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The second characterization in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacterizationOfAbelianLocalGroups"}
              implies that
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi T
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}_T \otimes -)
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#localization_of_spectra Localization of spectra
          #TLocalSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-local
              (or
              = succeed "-local," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              are
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TLocalGroup"}
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-localization
              of a spectrum is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} reflection
              into
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-localization," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TLocalSpectrum"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\mathbb{Z}_T)
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Bauer11"} Bauer 11, Example 1.7
            %p
              It can also be constructed as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
              where we invert the maps that induce an isomorphism on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}_T
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                  \-homology isomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+localization"} homology localization
          %h3#localization_of_nilpotent_spaces Localization of nilpotent spaces
          %p
            The presence of the nonabelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
            makes the theory of localization of unstable spaces more subtle than that of spectra. If spaces are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+spaces"} simple spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
            is abelian and acts trivially on the higher homotopy groups. Even more generally, it suffices to consider
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+spaces"} nilpotent spaces
          %p
            For a nilpotent space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-local
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#MayPonto"} May-Ponto, Theorem 6.1.1
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Whenever
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
                induces an isomorphism on homology with
                = succeed "-coefficients," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Y,Z] \to [X,Z]
                is a bijection.
            %li
              %p
                Each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(Z)
                is a
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p
                Each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+group"} homology group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(Z,\mathbb{Z})
                is a
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            For a general nilpotent space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:X\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            nilpotent and
            = succeed "-local," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              \-localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#MayPonto"} May-Ponto, Theorem 6.1.2
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The induced map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Y,Z] \to [X,Z]
                is a bijection for all
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                induces an isomorphism on homology with
                = succeed "-coefficients." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
            %li
              %p
                The induced map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X) \to \pi_n(Y)
                is an algebraic
                = succeed "-localization" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                The induced map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(X,\mathbb{Z}) \to H_n(Y,\mathbb{Z})
                is an algebraic
                = succeed "-localization" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h3#localization_of_nonnilpotent_spaces Localization of non-nilpotent spaces
          %p
            For non-nilpotent spaces, there are multiple inequivalent definitions of localization (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MayPonto"} May-Ponto, Remark 19.3.11
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                One can do a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
                with respect to the class of
                = succeed "-homology" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Y,Z] \to [X,Z]
                is an isomorphism for all
                = succeed "-homology" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
                (the first characterization of
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p
                One can construct a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totalization"} totalization
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
                induced by the “free simplicial
                = succeed "-module\u201D" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#BousfieldKan72"} Bousfield-Kan
            %li
              %p
                One can do a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
                with respect to the maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:S^1\to S^1
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in \neg T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#CasacubertaPeschke"} Casacuberta-Peschke
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
                is a
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-local+module"} locally
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X)
          %p
            One can of course state the other two characterizations of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            \-local space” from the nilpotent case even in the non-nilpotent case, as is done by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sullivan70"} Sullivan
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToCompletion Relation to formal completion
          #RelationToCompletion.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              %strong (relation to completion)
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\{p\}
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                  \-acyclic
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to X
              out of a
              = succeed "-acyclic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+homotopy"} null homotopic
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              \-local spectra are also known as
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-complete
              spectra, and are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
              at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+spectrum"} Moore spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Bauer11"} Bauer 11, Example 1.7
            %p
              This may be regarded as a consequence of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mod+p+Whitehead+theorem"} mod p Whitehead theorem
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#MayPonto"}> May-Ponto, example 19.2.3
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie, example 8
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LurieProper"} Lurie “Proper morphisms”, section 4
          %p In summary:
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} localization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+space"} of spaces/spectra
                at
